  "step_3": "The decision reason requires considering the probability of obtaining a favorable outcome (≥2400 Euros) and preferring the lottery with the higher such probability. In this case, Lottery A has a 100% chance of a favorable outcome, while Lottery B has a 99% chance. Thus, the reason would prefer A. However, the individual’s verbal report does not mention probability of favorable outcomes at all. Instead, the individual focuses on the small monetary difference (100 euros) and the risk of getting zero, treating that as negligible. There is no reference to comparing probabilities of favorable outcomes or to the rule that favors higher probability of favorable outcomes. Therefore, the individual did not use the decision reason as specified. The information considered (differences in outcomes and risk of zero) differs from the required information (probability of favorable outcomes). The justification (negligibility of differences) does not align with the rule (prefer higher probability of favorable outcome).",
